{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review & increase funding for research into Type 1 diabetes cure",
        "additional_details": "Increased public funding should be provided to the NHS & NIHR to explore trials & international partnerships to accelerate research towards lasting insulin independence.\r\n \r\nType 1 diabetes is a lifelong condition that requires daily insulin and constant monitoring. Although promising advances are being made in research aimed at achieving lasting insulin independence, we feel more investment is needed to accelerate progress towards a cure. We believe the Government should review current public funding for Type 1 diabetes cure research, identify gaps and increase investment to support promising research, clinical trials and international collaboration. This should help advance the search for a lasting cure for children and adults living with Type 1 diabetes.",
        "background": "We ask the Government to review current public funding in Type 1 diabetes cure research, identify funding gaps and increase investment to advance promising research into a cure.",
